  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 9bc4902ccea98cf44865aecb61fc1ff4, type: 3}
  m_Name: Mariam
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::SuspectData
  FirstName: Mariam
  LastName: Beridze
  Nickname: Miri
  Occupation: Student
  CharacterDescription: "A typical teen girl with a harsh attitude. Studies hard to become a doctor. Has a mom, dad, and a sister; Sharena is her mom. She tries hard to gain her teacher and mom's love \u2014 an overachiever raised under a harsh mother. Has a special interest in human anatomy."
  CharacterArc: "When mutated, Miriam becomes fully nonverbal \u2014 creepy and deeply unsettling. She screams with an extremely disturbing voice if asked too many questions. She can manipulate the environment, moving, shattering, spotting, and opening things with startling speed. Physical mutations include a broken neck, black goop dripping from her face, and large tumorous hands."
  DateOfBirth: 03/09/1972
  Sex: Female
  EntryPermitExpiryDate: 18 MAY
  IsResident: 1
  GivesPaperwork: 1
  handwritingFont: {fileID: 0}
  startingInfectionScore: 0
  dailyInfectionProgression: {x: 8, y: 18}
  alterEgoName: The Anatomist
  basePersonalityDescriptors:
  - Meticulous and high-strung; treats every checkpoint interaction like an exam she cannot fail.
  - Redirects personal questions toward schoolwork or her mother's expectations.
  - Speaks with clinical precision whenever the topic turns to anatomy or medicine.
  - Visibly tenses at any implication that she has fallen short.
  normalBehaviorNotes: Presents as a driven, slightly brittle student who over-explains herself. Answers quickly and precisely, often citing grades or her mother's standards as justification. Becomes noticeably rigid when questioned about home life; softens only when allowed to talk about her studies, particularly anatomy.
  fullMutantDialogue: {fileID: 11400000, guid: be9c05fa596d1a14ba5b58d5d887bae3, type: 2}
  replacementIDPhoto: {fileID: 0}
  IDPhoto: {fileID: 2800000, guid: 11f445b9376d6d64b9ad9d0ac1ee5a48, type: 3}
  CharacterPrefab: {fileID: 947284972480981435, guid: 44cfb9d2070b2ab45ac3e84ef713a834, type: 3}
  entryReasons:
    earlyDaysReasons:
    - Clinic tutoring. Mother expects me by six.
    - Stayed late to redo an exam.
    - Library run before it closes.
    midDaysReasons:
    - Back from the clinic volunteer program.
    - Studying with a classmate. Mother dislikes lateness.
    - Collecting textbooks before lessons stopped.
    finalDaysReasons:
    - Going home. Nowhere else worth going.
    - Studying in the empty old clinic.
    - Home. Mother will ask what I learned.
  invalidEntryReasons:
    earlyDaysReasons:
    - Home from my bakery job. I left school.
    - Home to my aunt. She raised me.
    - Skipped tutoring for a film. Mother lets me.
    midDaysReasons:
    - Quit the ward. Becoming a hairdresser.
    - Back from my post office job.
    - Out late on purpose. Mother never asks.
    finalDaysReasons:
    - Going home to my husband.
    - Going to sleep. I quit studying.
    - Collecting my nurse's pension.
  entryDialogues:
    lastVerdict: 0
    dialoguesEarlyDays:
    - Here. Everything is organised by date, in case that helps.
    - My mother says punctuality reflects character. I will not be late.
    dialoguesMidDays:
    - The line was longer yesterday. I timed it. This is faster.
    - I have a test tomorrow. I would like to be efficient.
    dialoguesFinalDays:
    - My sister is waiting. Please, I have done everything correctly.
    - Why does this take longer every day? I follow every instruction.
  uncannyEntryDialogues:
    lastVerdict: 0
    dialoguesEarlyDays:
    - I checked everything. I think. I don't remember checking it.
    - My hands won't stay still. I'm not usually like this.
    dialoguesMidDays:
    - I can hear my own heartbeat. Is that normal? Is it?
    - My mother cannot see me like this. She can't.
    dialoguesFinalDays:
    - Something under my skin isn't mine. I shouldn't have said that.
    - Just tell me if I did something wrong. Please.
  exitDialoguesPassed:
    lastVerdict: 1
    dialoguesEarlyDays:
    - Thank you. I'll tell my mother it went well.
    dialoguesMidDays:
    - See? I told you everything was in order.
    dialoguesFinalDays:
    - I can still make it home before dark. Thank you.
  exitDialoguesQuarantined:
    lastVerdict: 2
    dialoguesEarlyDays: []
    dialoguesMidDays: []
    dialoguesFinalDays: []
  exitDialoguesKilled:
    lastVerdict: 3
    dialoguesEarlyDays: []
    dialoguesMidDays: []
    dialoguesFinalDays: []
  quarantineExitLines:
  - I would like to keep my study schedule with me.
  - Someone must tell my mother. She will not handle this.
  killExitLines:
  - I was going to be a doctor. A good one.
  - My mother will say I brought this on myself.
