  introDialogue: {fileID: 11400000, guid: ada4737c1145afd48aa7b3b5855249f5, type: 2}
  questionResponses:
  - question: Where are you coming from?
    earlyDaysAnswer: The clinic. Anatomy tutoring, then the volunteer ward. Home by six.
    midDaysAnswer: The clinic. The volunteer program still runs. Rolling bandages is still practice.
    finalDaysAnswer: The old clinic building. Mostly empty now. Quieter than home for studying.
    mismatchEarlyDaysAnswer: The medical institute. I'm in my third year. Surgery, eventually.
    mismatchMidDaysAnswer: Home. I'm an only child, so it's quiet enough to study.
    mismatchFinalDaysAnswer: The textile factory canteen. I gave up medicine long ago.
    uncannyEarlyDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyMidDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyFinalDaysAnswer: 
    cameraTrigger: 
  - question: Are you experiencing any symptoms?
    earlyDaysAnswer: No. I sleep too little, but from studying. I know the difference.
    midDaysAnswer: Headaches. Reading by candle in the power cuts. Not a symptom.
    finalDaysAnswer: Cold hands. Little sleep. I took my own pulse. It is normal.
    mismatchEarlyDaysAnswer: Nothing. I haven't opened a textbook in weeks. No eye strain.
    mismatchMidDaysAnswer: No. My mother lets me rest whenever. She says grades don't matter.
    mismatchFinalDaysAnswer: I wouldn't know. Blood makes me faint. I can't take a pulse.
    uncannyEarlyDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyMidDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyFinalDaysAnswer: 
    cameraTrigger: 
  idleBarks:
    earlyDays:
    - The body survives remarkably specific traumas. It's fascinating, honestly.
    - I don't usually get nervous. I don't know why I'm nervous.
    midDays:
    - Does medical school account for checkpoint delays? I doubt it.
    - I notice things about the body I never used to. Studies, probably.
    finalDays:
    - My sister asked if I was scared. Fear isn't useful information.
    - I keep counting things. I don't know when I started.
    uncannyEarlyDays: []
    uncannyMidDays: []
    uncannyFinalDays: []
  IDNumber: 5127493
